WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.880
Welcome to Grade 4 English, Unit 6: People in Society.

2
00:00:04.680 --> 00:00:05.900
Welcome to Unit 6!

3
00:00:06.600 --> 00:00:13.080
This unit is all about the people in our society — the many
workers, leaders, and helpers who make a community work.

4
00:00:13.600 --> 00:00:18.040
You will meet engineers and carpenters,
governors and senators, artists and photographers,

5
00:00:18.580 --> 00:00:21.960
and you will learn about refugees,
immigrants, and the roles we all play.

6
00:00:22.660 --> 00:00:27.980
Along the way you will use the Present Simple to describe
jobs, should and mustn't to give advice and rules,

7
00:00:27.980 --> 00:00:31.340
and question words to interview people about their work.

8
00:00:32.000 --> 00:00:38.440
By the end, you will be able to describe the helpers in
your own town — just like Sarah does in this unit's story,

9
00:00:38.820 --> 00:00:40.000
“The Community Parade”.

10
00:00:40.820 --> 00:00:46.200
In this short lecture, preview the key
ideas and prepare for the independent lesson.

11
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:48.360
By the end of this unit,

12
00:00:48.820 --> 00:00:53.660
you will be able to name and describe at least
twenty jobs and roles that people play in society.

13
00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:59.200
you will also explain what different workers
and leaders do, using the present simple.

14
00:01:00.140 --> 00:01:03.920
you will also give advice and state
rules using should and mustn't.

15
00:01:04.360 --> 00:01:06.240
Keep these goals in mind as you work.

16
00:01:06.760 --> 00:01:13.280
Your vocabulary work begins with these words: janitor,
carpenter, laborer, engineer, merchant, governor.

17
00:01:14.200 --> 00:01:19.040
Listen to each pronunciation in the
vocabulary lab, study its meaning in context,

18
00:01:19.520 --> 00:01:22.660
and use the word accurately in
your own discussion and writing.

19
00:01:23.610 --> 00:01:29.800
The reading sequence includes The People of Our
Town and Two Neighbours: A Refugee and an Immigrant.

20
00:01:30.840 --> 00:01:31.860
Read actively.

21
00:01:32.720 --> 00:01:37.320
Identify each text's central ideas,
notice viewpoint and reliability,

22
00:01:37.880 --> 00:01:41.440
and support every inference with
relevant evidence from the text.

23
00:01:42.260 --> 00:01:44.900
The first language focus is Present Simple.

24
00:01:45.800 --> 00:01:50.660
We use the Present Simple to talk about routines,
facts, and things that happen again and again.

25
00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:55.420
It is perfect for describing jobs,
because most jobs are the same every day:

26
00:01:56.140 --> 00:01:58.380
“The janitor cleans the school every morning.”

27
00:01:59.200 --> 00:02:05.160
Notice the structure in the model examples, then apply
it deliberately in connected sentences and paragraphs.

28
00:02:06.220 --> 00:02:10.080
In speaking, you will complete Speaking 1: Describe a Job.

29
00:02:10.330 --> 00:02:15.080
Organise your ideas, use evidence
and respond clearly to questions.

30
00:02:15.880 --> 00:02:18.960
In writing, you will plan, draft, check and revise.

31
00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:22.620
Use the success criteria before submitting your work.

32
00:02:22.980 --> 00:02:24.400
You are ready to begin.

33
00:02:24.900 --> 00:02:30.440
Start with the vocabulary lab, continue through
reading and comprehension, apply the grammar focus,

34
00:02:30.860 --> 00:02:32.980
and complete the speaking and writing practices.

35
00:02:33.680 --> 00:02:38.420
Use AI English for hints and feedback, and
bring your questions to the live sessions.
